# Mova — Environment Variable & Authentication Configuration Template
# Copy this file to .env and fill in your real values.
#
# Variables prefixed with EXPO_PUBLIC_ are embedded into the JS bundle and exposed
# to the mobile client and browser. NEVER put service-role keys or database passwords here.

# ===================================================================
# 1. Supabase Client Configuration
# ===================================================================
# Find these values in: Supabase Dashboard → Project Settings → API
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-id.supabase.co
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-publishable-anon-key-here

# ===================================================================
# 2. Supabase Dashboard URL & Redirect Settings (External Setup)
# ===================================================================
# In Supabase Dashboard → Authentication → URL Configuration:
#
# Site URL:
#   - For development: http://localhost:8081
#   - For production:  https://your-production-domain.com
#
# Redirect URLs (must include):
#   - mova://auth/callback                     (iOS & Android native deep link)
#   - http://localhost:8081/auth/callback       (Local web dev)
#   - https://your-production-domain.com/auth/callback (Production web)

# ===================================================================
# 3. Google OAuth Setup (External Setup)
# ===================================================================
# 1. In Google Cloud Console (https://console.cloud.google.com/):
#    - Create an OAuth 2.0 Client ID (Application type: "Web application").
#    - Set "Authorized JavaScript origins":
#        https://your-project-id.supabase.co
#    - Set "Authorized redirect URIs":
#        https://your-project-id.supabase.co/auth/v1/callback
# 2. In Supabase Dashboard → Authentication → Providers → Google:
#    - Enable the Google provider.
#    - Enter the Client ID and Client Secret from Google Cloud Console.

# ===================================================================
# 4. Apple OAuth Setup (External Setup)
# ===================================================================
# 1. In Apple Developer Account (https://developer.apple.com/):
#    - Register an App ID and a Services ID for Sign in with Apple.
#    - In Services ID configuration, add Primary App ID, Domain:
#        your-project-id.supabase.co
#    - Set Return URL:
#        https://your-project-id.supabase.co/auth/v1/callback
#    - Generate a private key (.p8) with Sign in with Apple enabled.
# 2. In Supabase Dashboard → Authentication → Providers → Apple:
#    - Enable the Apple provider.
#    - Enter the Services ID, Team ID, Key ID, and upload the private key (.p8).

# ===================================================================
# 5. Server Secrets (NEVER EMBED IN MOBILE APP)
# ===================================================================
# Keep these strictly out of the mobile client. For CI/CD or backend scripts only:
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=never-commit-this
# DATABASE_URL=never-commit-this

